ommission over illegal contributions days before the election", "Open seat in a Democratic-leaning state with a favorable environment; independent Rick Bennett trails in money"], "rationale": "Polling from September through mid-October consistently gave Pingree an eight-to-thirteen-point lead, raters call the race Safe or Likely Democratic, and markets price her near 95%, but a late-October poll showing a tie justifies shading the forecast well below the polling average. Charles's ethics fine and Maine's Democratic lean still leave Pingree clearly favored.", "watch": "Whether additional final surveys confirm the late tie or the race reverts to the double-digit Democratic margin seen through mid-October.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Janet Mills (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Hannah Pingree enters the final week favored to keep the governorship in Democratic hands after two terms of Janet Mills, who is term-limited. Polls from September and mid-October consistently showed Pingree ahead by eight to thirteen points, most race raters call the contest Safe or Likely Democratic, and betting markets price a Democratic win around 95 percent. The state's Democratic lean and a favorable national environment reinforce that edge.\n\nThe picture is not entirely settled. A poll released in the final days of October reported Pingree and Republican Bobby Charles tied, a sharp break from earlier surveys, and the race has been described as low-key. Charles also took a hit when the state Ethics Commission fined his campaign more than $22,000 over illegal contributions. Independent Rick Bennett is on the ballot but trails badly in fundraising, and Maine's ranked-choice voting limits any spoiler effect.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9757, "margin": 10.9}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9716, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9705, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9685, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-0